Z||000000||Eric_PA||11-09-2000||06:33 AM||||I was wondering about a clutch pedal from a 1987 4 cylinder Fiero. Is it the kind to get. What I mean is that I heard some of the pedals were made out of aluminum and don't hold up. I was wondering since I allready got the whole pedal assemblyy out of the 87. I am doing this because I am performing an engine swap with a Quad 4, and currently have a rat-matic Fiero. Thanks in advance.<P>Eric<BR>86.5 Black Fastback||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||11-09-2000||07:05 AM||||Eric, from what I seen here the 87-88 clutch pedals were the ones to get. I have one out of an 87 and it is steel.<P>If you already have the pedal you can see if it is steel by seeing if a magnet sticks to it.<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 11-09-2000).]||||reg||1
